# Testing Strategy Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish testing practices for all application layers. While testing approaches may vary by component type, core testing principles remain consistent.

## Best Practices
- Follow the Testing Pyramid: unit > integration > UI
- Write tests before implementing features (TDD)
- Test both success and failure cases
- Keep tests independent and isolated
- Mock external dependencies and services
- Use descriptive test names following "should_when_given" pattern
- Focus on testing behavior, not implementation
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions
- Maintain test data separate from test logic

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize test files to mirror source structure
- Name test files with `_test.dart` suffix
- Group related tests with descriptive block names
- Structure test files as:
  ```
  test/
    unit/
      domain/
        usecases/
        repositories/
      data/
        repositories/
        datasources/
    integration/
      repositories/
      services/
    widget/
      screens/
      components/
    goldens/
      screens/
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use AAA pattern (Arrange-Act-Assert)
- Implement helper methods for common setup
- Follow naming convention: `test('should <expected behavior> when <condition>')`
- Use mocks for dependencies with `mockito` or `mocktail`
- Keep test files focused on a single class/component
- Use `setUp` and `tearDown` for common initialization
- Prefer `expect` over `assert` statements

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Group related tests to reduce setup/teardown overhead
- Mock heavy dependencies for unit tests
- Use test fakes for complex systems
- Implement benchmarking tests for performance-critical paths
- Use parameterized tests for testing multiple inputs
- Keep unit tests fast (milliseconds, not seconds)
- Avoid unnecessary widget rebuilds in UI tests

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test repositories with mock data sources
- Test BLoCs with mock repositories
- Test widgets with mock BLoCs
- Use golden tests for UI verification
- Implement integration tests for critical user flows
- Test offline behavior and error recovery
- Verify analytics and logging implementations
- Test localization and accessibility compliance


